7. States and local governments\n\nThe question asks about \"average level of holdings of treasury bills that had regular weekly and annual maturings exceeding $200 million USD par values in January 1981.\"\n\n\nI notice the table provides a detailed breakdown for the Jan. 1981 treasury bills, revealing specific holdings across different investor categories. Most categories show minimal or zero holdings, with the highest amounts held by U.S. Government accounts and Federal Reserve banks at $756 million, followed by commercial banks at $558 million.\n\nThe data reveals a nuanced breakdown of Treasury bill holdings across different investor types, highlighting significant variations in investment分布.\n\nI'll analyze the average levels across various investor categories, focusing on identifying which groups exceed the $200 million threshold.\n\nThe data reveals a clear pattern: most investor categories have holdings below $200 million, with only two categories surpassing this limit - U.S. Government accounts and Federal Reserve banks at $756 million, and commercial banks at $558 million.\n\nThis means exactly 2 categories meet the specified criterion, representing a precise measurement of investor engagement in this financial instrument.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_5784e47553fe4f02b949ad4f","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"todo__todo_write","arguments":{"content":"- [x] Examine the Treasury Bulletin resource files to understand the data structure\n- [x] Find the Treasury Ownership Survey data for end of January 1980\n- [x] Identify the investor categories and their holdings of treasury bills\n- [x] Determine which categories had average holdings exceeding $200 million USD par values in January 1981\n- [x] Count the categories meeting this criterion\n- [ ] Write the answer to /app/answer.txt"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"todo"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
